   "subject": "total density across groups",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Hello,<div>When one models differences between groups of animals (say sexes) using an individual covariate and the conditional likelihood, it is easy to obtain either group-specific or total densities, with associated measures of uncertainty using derived().</div><div><br></div><div>Is there also an easy way to get total densities with associated measures of uncertainty if one models these differences as groups using the full likelihood (e.g. using predict())?</div><div><br></div><div>Thanks,</div><div>Eric</div></div>"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "th7UzOS2CQAJ",
   "from": "Murray Efford",
   "author": "118cea91a1619106",
   "date": "2018-04-11T21:09:38Z",
   "subject": "Re: total density across groups",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div>Hello there<br></div>An interesting challenge while I \r\nchew on my breakfast muesli! I think you can do it by specifying \r\nthe contrasts used to code levels of the group factor.<br><br>From a vignette coming soon to a CRAN mirror near you...<br><br><img src=\"https://groups.google.com/group/secrgroup/attach/9b6e4ccd41eb6/Auto%20Generated%20Inline%20Image%201?part=0.1\" alt=\"\"><br>Footnote 10 says &#39;this also works in secr&#39;. Try running the following code. Note x 2 (number of groups) scales mean to total.<br>Murray<br><br> <br><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border-color:rgb(187,187,187);border-style:solid;border-width:1px\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#000\">library</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">secr</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br><br></span><span style=\"color:#800\">## generate some fake groups and fit model</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>covariates</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">captdata</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> data</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">frame</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">sex </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> sample</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">c</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&#39;F&#39;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&#39;M&#39;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">),</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> nrow</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">captdata</span><span style=\"color:#660\">),</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> p </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> c</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#066\">0.4</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#066\">0.6</span><span style=\"color:#660\">),</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> replace </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> TRUE</span><span style=\"color:#660\">))</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>fitg </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> secr</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">fit</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">captdata</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> model </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> D</span><span style=\"color:#660\">~</span><span style=\"color:#000\">g</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> groups </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#080\">&#39;sex&#39;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#800\">## refit model with contrasts</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>fitgt </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> secr</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">fit</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">captdata</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> model</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\">D</span><span style=\"color:#660\">~</span><span style=\"color:#000\">g</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> groups </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#080\">&#39;sex&#39;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> details </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> list</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">contrasts</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\">list</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">g </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> contr</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">sum</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)))</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br><br></span><span style=\"color:#800\">## checking results...</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#800\">## same likelihood</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>AIC</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">fitg</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> fitgt</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#800\">## different coefficients</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>coef</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">fitg</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>coef</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">fitgt</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#800\">## same group-specific estimates</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>predict</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">fitg</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>predict</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">fitgt</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br><br></span><span style=\"color:#800\">## now compare estimates of total density</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#800\">## sum of group-specific densities</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>sum</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">sapply</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">predict</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">fitg</span><span style=\"color:#660\">),</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#080\">&#39;[[&#39;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#080\">&#39;D&#39;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#080\">&#39;estimate&#39;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">))</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#800\">## backtransformed from recoded</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>exp</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">coef</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">fitgt</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)[</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&#39;D&#39;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&#39;beta&#39;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">])</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#660\">*</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#066\">2</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br><br></span><span style=\"color:#800\">## using identity link to dodge back-transformation bias</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>fitgi </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> secr</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">fit</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">captdata</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> model </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> D</span><span style=\"color:#660\">~</span><span style=\"color:#000\">g</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> groups </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#080\">&#39;sex&#39;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> link </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> list</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">D</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&#39;identity&#39;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">))</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>fitgti </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> secr</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">fit</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">captdata</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> model</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\">D</span><span style=\"color:#660\">~</span><span style=\"color:#000\">g</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> groups </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#080\">&#39;sex&#39;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> details </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> list</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">contrasts</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\">list</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">g </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> contr</span><span style=\"color:#660\">.</span><span style=\"color:#000\">sum</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)),</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> link </span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> list</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">D</span><span style=\"color:#660\">=</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&#39;identity&#39;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">))</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#800\">## sum of group-specific densities</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>sum</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">sapply</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">predict</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">fitgi</span><span style=\"color:#660\">),</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#080\">&#39;[[&#39;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#080\">&#39;D&#39;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#080\">&#39;estimate&#39;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">))</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br></span><span style=\"color:#800\">## backtransformed from recoded</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br>coef</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#000\">fitgti</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)[</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&#39;D&#39;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\">c</span><span style=\"color:#660\">(</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&#39;beta&#39;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#080\">&#39;lcl&#39;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">,</span><span style=\"color:#080\">&#39;ucl&#39;</span><span style=\"color:#660\">)]*</span><span style=\"color:#066\">2</span><span style=\"color:#000\"><br><br></span></div></code></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<br><br><br><br>On Thursday, April 12, 2018 at 8:13:13 AM UTC+12, Eric H wrote:<blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0;margin-left:0.8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\">Hello,<div>When one models differences between groups of animals (say sexes) using an individual covariate and the conditional likelihood, it is easy to obtain either group-specific or total densities, with associated measures of uncertainty using derived().</div><div><br></div><div>Is there also an easy way to get total densities with associated measures of uncertainty if one models these differences as groups using the full likelihood (e.g. using predict())?</div><div><br></div><div>Thanks,</div><div>Eric</div></div></blockquote>"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "Wa2Fc-HxCQAJ",
   "from": "Eric H",
   "author": "0dbfcf0efe4ff8fe",
   "date": "2018-04-12T15:10:35Z",
   "subject": "Re: total density across groups",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Good day Murray,<div><br></div><p style=\"text-align:center;clear:both\"></p><div>Thanks for this. With my own (preliminary) data and the log link function, the back-transformed total density (0.001301094) was very similar to the sum of group-specific densities (0.00130501). I didn&#39;t try the identity link fix, but would try it if we decide to go this way. I may still go with the CL and derived(), because we will again be fitting many models to many data sets, so it would be nice if we didn&#39;t have to fit the same model twice.  However, it&#39;s very helpful to have this handy. There may be situations where we want to fit models with spatial covariates of density, so would need to use the FL and model sexes as different groups or sessions. </div><div><br></div><div>All the best,</div><div>Eric</div><div><br></div></div>"
    ]
   ]
  }
 ]
